<title>UK: UK grain futures close higher on thin market.</title>
<headline>UK grain futures close higher on thin market.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK grain futures closed slightly higher on Friday but business was thin.</p>
<p>&quot;People don't seem to know where to go from here and the market has just been drifting,&quot; said a trader.</p>
<p>Wheat futures closed 0.30 to 0.50 stg up after trading 266 lots while barley was unchanged to 0.50 stg higher on 30 lots.</p>
<p>In Amsterdam the milling wheat futures were five marks down on a turnover of four lots.</p>
<p>--Jim Ballantyne, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8062</p>
</text>
